    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[What AI Is Bad at?]]></title>
        <id>https://laike9m.com/blog/what-ai-is-bad-at,174/</id>
        <link href="https://laike9m.com/blog/what-ai-is-bad-at,174/"/>
        <updated>2026-11-22T06:07:57.000Z</updated>
        <summary type="html"><![CDATA[为什么 AI 几乎统治了所有智力活动，却还没在投资上打败人类？文章以全美投资大赛（USIC）最新成绩为引子，提出「简单输入→复杂输出」与「复杂输入→简单输出」的四象限框架，解释 AI 为何在围棋、编程、数学上已彻底超越人类，却在面对开放、复杂的真实世界输入时仍显不足。投资只是表象，真正的问题是：当输入不再有限且可离散化时，人类的经验、直觉与对异常的敏感仍具独特优势。

Why hasn’t AI beaten humans at investing, even as it dominates almost every other intellectual domain? Using recent US Investing Championship results as a starting point, this essay introduces a simple 2×2 framework of input/output complexity. It explains why AI has thoroughly surpassed humans in “simple input → complex output” tasks like Go, programming, and math, yet still struggles with open-ended, complex real-world inputs—of which investing is a prime example.]]></summary>
        <author>
            <name>laike9m's blog</name>
        </author>
    </entry>
